        "sharedSolutionDiagramId": "p34-q6-sum-solution",
        "answer": {
          "short": null,
          "worked": "Plot $y=x$ and $y=2^x$ on the same axes in DESMOS, then plot $y=x+2^x$. The vertical distance between the sum curve and the line is $2^x$, so the sum curve stays above the line.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q6a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What do you notice about the graph of $y=x$ and $y=x+2^x$ as $x\\to-\\infty$?\n\nThis is called an oblique asymptote. Explain your observation.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q6a-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " is an oblique asymptote. The sum curve approaches this line from above as ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\to-\\infty",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", because the vertical separation ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(x+2^x)-x=2^x\\to0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "As $x\\to-\\infty$, $2^x\\to0$. The vertical separation is $(x+2^x)-x=2^x$, which tends to zero. Therefore the sum curve approaches the line $y=x$ from above, and $y=x$ is an oblique asymptote.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
